# God's Eye View — environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in what you want. On macOS the launcher can also read
# keys from the Keychain (see README); on Linux/Windows use this file or env vars.
#
# EVERY KEY IN THIS FILE IS OPTIONAL AND FREE. The app boots and runs with an
# empty .env: it starts on the keyless satellite globe and every layer that
# needs no account is live. The keys below unlock layers or improve the globe —
# none of them require a billing account or a credit card.
#
# The two exceptions are called out explicitly under "METERED" at the bottom.
# They are off by default and the app never reaches for them unset.
#
# NOTE ON CLIENT-EXPOSED KEYS: CESIUM_ION_TOKEN (and GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY, if you
# opt in) are injected into the browser bundle by design — they are used
# client-side and WILL be visible in devtools. Restrict/scope them at the
# provider rather than trying to hide them (see SECURITY.md). All other keys
# below stay server-side.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GLOBE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: Cesium ion token — the single biggest visual upgrade.
# Unlocks the Bing Aerial / Bing Labels map stacks, Cesium World Terrain, and
# Cesium OSM Buildings (3D building massing on every globe stack), which is this
# build's free stand-in for Google's photogrammetric mesh.
#
# Free tier: individual NON-COMMERCIAL use, 5 GB storage + 15 GB streaming/month.
# No credit card. Create a token scoped to `assets:read` over assets 1, 2, 3 and
# 96188 at https://ion.cesium.com → Access Tokens.
# CLIENT-EXPOSED.
#
# Without it the globe still works: the keyless `satellite` stack (Sentinel-2
# cloudless, 10 m) plus keyless Re:Earth terrain, and no 3D buildings.
CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=

# Optional override for the keyless imagery source backing the `satellite` stack.
# Unset (default) = Sentinel-2 cloudless by EOX — 10 m, but CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, so
#   NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY.
# `gibs` = NASA GIBS Blue Marble — coarse (~600 m) but U.S. public domain with no
#   usage restriction. Set this for any commercial deployment.
# The app also falls back to GIBS on its own if EOX is unreachable.
# GEV_KEYLESS_IMAGERY=gibs

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LIVE LAYERS (all free, no credit card)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: TomTom live traffic flow. Free tier is 200,000 tile requests/MONTH
# with no credit card — get a key at https://developer.tomtom.com.
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY: the browser fetches same-origin /api/tomtom/* and never sees
# the key. Without a key the traffic layer runs its built-in simulation, which
# labels itself SIMULATED and never claims to be live.
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=

# Soft cap on upstream tile fetches per UTC MONTH (default 180000).
# Sized ~10% under TomTom's free monthly allowance so ordinary use can never
# cross into a billable state. Over the cap the proxy serves cached/stale tiles
# instead of hitting upstream.
# NOTE: this replaced a per-DAY budget. The old TOMTOM_DAILY_TILE_BUDGET is
# still honoured if set (read as a daily rate and projected across 31 days), but
# its former 40,000/day default was ~6x the free monthly allowance.
# TOMTOM_MONTHLY_TILE_BUDGET=180000

# Optional: NASA FIRMS live active fires. SERVER-SIDE ONLY (never reaches the
# browser — the client polls the /api/firms proxy). Free key, no account:
# https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# Without a key the FIRMS Active Fires layer is empty ("KEY REQUIRED").
# FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# Optional: Live AIS vessels layer.
# Browser fetch path. Keep same-origin so the private stream key stays server-side.
VITE_AIS_LIVE_API_URL=/api/ais-live
# Client render cap. The server can keep a larger AISStream cache, but drawing
# every global vessel at once can overwhelm WebGL on laptops.
VITE_AIS_LIVE_MAX_ROWS=12000
# Active label cap after screen-space clustering. Labels exist for all rendered
# ships, but only clustered winners are shown to keep text readable.
VITE_AIS_LIVE_LABEL_MAX_ROWS=900
# Private AISStream key for the server-side websocket (free, no credit card:
# https://aisstream.io). Do not prefix with VITE_. Without it the Vessels layer
# is empty.
AISSTREAM_API_KEY=
# Optional AISStream subscription filters.
# AISSTREAM_BOUNDING_BOXES=[[[-90,-180],[90,180]]]
# AISSTREAM_MESSAGE_TYPES=PositionReport,StandardClassBPositionReport,ExtendedClassBPositionReport,ShipStaticData,StaticDataReport
# Feed watchdog: silence (ms) after which the feed is REPORTED stale; the socket
# is recycled at 2.5x that. Default 120000. The watchdog self-arms only for the
# default worldwide subscription — a narrow filter above can be legitimately
# quiet, so set this explicitly (sized for your filter) to opt back in.
# 0 disables the silence watch entirely.
# AISSTREAM_SILENCE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Optional: OpenSky auth mode (oauth | basic | auto | anon)
# Default: oauth — requires client credentials below.
# Set to "anon" to skip aircraft auth (rate-limited but works). Basic auth was
# retired upstream in March 2026; OAuth client credentials are the current path.
OPENSKY_AUTH_MODE=oauth

# Optional: OpenSky OAuth credentials (free account → Account → API Clients).
# Raises the daily flight-polling credit allowance. Anonymous works without.
OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: OpenSky credentials JSON file path (alternative to above)
# OPENSKY_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/path/to/credentials.json

# Optional: Mapillary access token — street-level fallback frames for CCTV
# cameras whose own upstream feed is down. Free, no credit card:
# https://www.mapillary.com/dashboard/developers → register an application.
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Imagery is CC BY-SA 4.0 and attributed in-app.
# Without it, a camera with a dead feed shows the honest UNAVAILABLE card.
# MAPILLARY_TOKEN=

# Optional: Launch Library 2 token — raises the Space Missions request
# allowance above the 15 calls/hour anonymous limit. Free.
# LL2_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: TfL app key — raises the rate limit on the London JamCams camera
# catalogue. The keyless endpoint works without it.
# TFL_APP_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CCTV layer tuning (advanced)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults are sensible — leave unset unless customizing the camera source pack.
# CCTV_SOURCES_FILE=config/cctv_sources.austin.json   # path to a source-pack JSON
# CCTV_SOURCES_JSON=                                   # inline source-pack JSON (overrides file)
# CCTV_AUSTIN_ROWS_URL=                                # override the Austin Open Data catalog URL
# CCTV_AUSTIN_MAX_SOURCES=36                           # cap cameras loaded from the Austin catalog
# CCTV_MAX_SOURCES=48                                  # overall cap on registered cameras
# CCTV_PREFER_AUSTIN=1                                 # prioritize Austin cameras in the registry
# CCTV_FORCE_AUSTIN=                                   # force Austin-only sources
# CCTV_AUTO_CALIBRATE=1                                # auto-calibrate camera projection (client flag)
# CCTV_DRAPE_MESH=1                                    # drape frames onto 3D geometry (client flag)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEV SERVER
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=4173
# Network binding. Default is localhost — the server is reachable ONLY from
# this machine. This is the safe default: the dev server brokers your
# configured API keys, so anyone who can reach it can spend your quota.
# LAN opt-in: set HOST=0.0.0.0 to share on your local network. WARNING: that
# exposes every key-brokering proxy to everyone on the network — use only on
# networks you trust.
# HOST=localhost
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# METERED — OFF BY DEFAULT. Setting either of these ends the zero-cost setup.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: Google Maps API key, for the Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles map
# stack ONLY. Nothing else in the app uses Google any more — geocoding, reverse
# geocoding and place search all run through the keyless /api/geocode,
# /api/reverse-geocode and /api/places/nearby proxies (Nominatim / Photon /
# Overpass).
#
# METERED: Photorealistic 3D Tiles is a Google Maps Platform ENTERPRISE SKU with
# ~1,000 free events/month and a required billing account; the subscription
# plans do not cover it. Unset, the `Google 3D` map-stack chip simply reads
# "Google Maps API key required" and the app defaults to the keyless satellite
# stack.
#
# ToS NOTE: Google's terms require Google's own geocoder alongside their tiles.
# This build geocodes through OpenStreetMap, so enabling this stack is your call
# to reconcile with Google's terms (see DATA_SOURCES.md). CLIENT-EXPOSED —
# restrict it (HTTP referrer + API restriction) in Google Cloud.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: OpenAI Realtime voice control + the AI HUD summary line.
# METERED. Unset, the mic button reports voice unavailable and the HUD shows its
# deterministic summary line instead — both are normal, supported states.
# Do not prefix with VITE_.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL=gpt-realtime-2
# Cheaper voice tier, used when the GEV MIC panel's MINI toggle is on.
# Model ids and prices are external facts that drift — if OpenAI moves this id,
# override it here rather than editing src/voice/voiceCost.js.
OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL_MINI=gpt-realtime-2.1-mini
OPENAI_REALTIME_VOICE=marin
OPENAI_REALTIME_REASONING_EFFORT=low
# Keep only a short conversational window. Current map state is fetched live.
OPENAI_REALTIME_CONTEXT_TOKENS=3000
OPENAI_REALTIME_CONTEXT_RETENTION=0.5
OPENAI_HUD_SUMMARY_MODEL=gpt-5-nano
# Optional: opt-in per-IP rate limit for the OpenAI cost endpoints
# (/api/realtime/token + /api/openai/hud-summary), in requests per minute.
# DEFAULT IS UNLIMITED — unset (or 0) means no throttling.
# Recommended whenever HOST is not localhost. NOTE: this is a per-IP,
# process-local guard (in-memory, resets on restart; over-limit requests get a
# sanitized 429) — it is NOT a billing cap. For hard spend protection set a
# provider-side budget: OpenAI platform -> Settings -> Limits (usage limits).
# GEV_RATELIMIT_OPENAI_PER_MIN=30

# Optional: Windy Webcams API — the CCTV layer's European coverage.
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY (frames are proxied through /api/cctv/frame).
# Free tier, no credit card: https://api.windy.com/keys  (key type: Webcams API)
# ~71k public cameras worldwide, ~7.7k in the European traffic category.
# Without it the CCTV layer still runs on the keyless Austin/Caltrans/TfL/
# Digitraffic packs — it just has no continental-Europe cameras.
# WINDY_WEBCAMS_KEY=
# CCTV_WINDY_MAX_SOURCES=320      # cap on Windy cameras in the registry
# CCTV_WINDY_INCLUDE_US=1         # 0 = Europe-only Windy coverage

# Optional: Fintraffic Digitraffic (Finland) — keyless, ~810 road cameras.
# CCTV_DIGITRAFFIC_ENABLED=1
# CCTV_DIGITRAFFIC_MAX_SOURCES=120

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  OSIRIS (the /osiris view) — ALL OPTIONAL
#  OSIRIS is free by design: aviation, maritime, satellites, fires, quakes,
#  news, CVEs and its 17,800-camera CCTV index all run on keyless public
#  feeds. These keys only widen it. Copy them into osiris/.env.local
#  (or leave them here — `npm run dev` passes this process's env to both).
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Cloudflare Radar — enables the "Internet Outages" + "Attack Origins" layers.
# Free: Cloudflare account -> My Profile -> API Tokens -> Custom token with
# permission "Account · Radar · Read". Without it those two layers stay hidden.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
#
# Etherscan — richer ETH wallet forensics in the CHAIN INTEL tab (free).
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=
#
# Helius — parsed Solana transfers (free). Without it SOL amounts stay blank.
# HELIUS_API_KEY=
#
# N2YO — satellite pass predictions (free, 1000 req/h).
# N2YO_API_KEY=
#
# RECON toolkit backend. Requires running OSIRIS's separate scanner service,
# which is NOT part of this repo — leave empty and the RECON tab returns 503.
# SCANNER_URL=
# SCANNER_KEY=

# Optional: N2YO — naked-eye satellite pass prediction.
# The app already predicts passes locally from CelesTrak TLEs via SGP4; N2YO
# adds ILLUMINATION (is the satellite sunlit while the observer is dark), which
# the local geometry does not model. Free, 1000 req/hour.
#   Get it: https://www.n2yo.com/login/register/  (then Profile)
# N2YO_API_KEY=
